# BestWorkplace — Windsurf Rules

Full rules in `/AGENTS.md`. Read it for any documentation-heavy task.

## Project
Documentation-only — no source code. xWiki 2.1 pages about agile leadership and workplace culture, published via GitHub Pages.
- `Docs/xwiki-pages/The Best Workplace/`: xWiki content pages (single source of truth)
- `Docs/xwiki-pages/scripts/`: Build and deployment scripts

## xWiki Syntax (2.1)
- Headings: `= H1 =`, `== H2 ==`, `=== H3 ===`
- Bold: `**bold**`, Italic: `//italic//`
- Links: `[[Link Text>>Space.Page]]`
- Diagrams: `{{mermaid}}...{{/mermaid}}`
- Full rules: `Docs/AGENTS/GlobalMasterKnowledge_for_xWiki.md`

## Commands
- Preview: `Docs\xwiki-pages\View.cmd`
- Build: `python Docs/xwiki-pages/scripts/build_ghpages.py`
- Deploy: `powershell Docs/xwiki-pages/scripts/deploy-ghpages.ps1`

## Safety
- No secrets in commits.
- No destructive git without explicit ask.
- Do not modify build output (`gh-pages-build/`) unless asked.
- Platform: Windows. PowerShell-compatible commands.

## Roles

When the user starts with "As \<Role\>" (e.g., "As Tech Writer, update…"), follow the **Role Activation Protocol** in `/AGENTS.md`. It tells you which role definition to load from `Docs/AGENTS/Multi_Agent_Collaboration_Rules.md` §2 and which documents to read.

**Context-budget note:** If loading all Required Reading exceeds Cascade's context window, load only the role entry from §2 and defer document reads until needed for the specific task.

## Agent Handoff
If a task exceeds Cascade context limits or needs deep reasoning, recommend:
- **Claude Code (Opus)**: complex multi-step reasoning
- **Cursor Composer**: multi-file edits with visual diff preview
See `/AGENTS.md` Agent Handoff Protocol for full reference.

## Conventions
- Commits: `type(scope): description`
- Solo developer + AI agents. Direct push to main is normal.
